The rule as written says the check's answer ought to move between these two texts. The docstring for recover_json_object states: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text". Since neither text has a code fence, the scored object is the last top-level object; changing the last object from {"b":2} to {"b":3} changes the recovered object, so the answer moves.